# Generic device profile: a PC or dev board with no headset attached.
# The sim services stand in for the hardware so the full OS stack runs
# anywhere - this is what makes "any hardware, x86 or arm" testable.
#
# HSVC_SVC_NAMES lists the service instances hsvcd's neighbours run.
# For each name <n>, HSVC_<N>_BIN is the driver binary and
# HSVC_<N>_ARGS its arguments. mkimage turns this into
# /etc/hibiscus/svc/<n>.env + an enabled hsvc-svc@<n>.service.
HSVC_SVC_NAMES="sim"
HSVC_SIM_BIN="/usr/bin/hsvc-sim"
HSVC_SIM_ARGS=""

# Stage the OpenXR runtime (monado + drv_hsvc) and enable the shell:
# monado.service + hibiscus-shell.service go live when mkimage has the
# xr artifacts (xr/build-runtime.sh out dir plus a dash-wayland build).
HSVC_XR=1
